{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["This month shall be to you the beginning of months, etc. — this accords with R. Yehoshua, who says the world was created in Nisan." "Of the months of the year — everywhere it says 'to you,' they are the eighth, ninth month relative to this one. And according to R. Eliezer, who says the world was created in Tishrei — the plain sense is essentially thus." "This month shall be to you — and even though it is not the beginning of months for the other nations, for you it shall be the beginning of months, to count sixth, seventh, eighth, ninth, twelfth month, which is the month of Adar. From it you count, for it to be a remembrance for you, because in it you went out of Egypt. And when the Torah says: ובחדש השביעי, it means relative to the month of the Exodus from Egypt. And so the verses customarily take their reckoning from the Exodus from Egypt, as it is written: בחדש השלישי לצאת בני ישראל וגו׳. And likewise regarding the building of the Temple: ויהי בשמונים שנה וד׳ מאות שנה לצאת בני ישראל מארץ מצרים."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {2 "The abbreviation יצ\"מ is resolved as יציאת מצרים (Exodus from Egypt)."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:41:09.998086972Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}